Z||000000||martin1875||11-11-2000||09:35 PM||||I HEAR ALOT OF PEOPLE TALKING A ABOUT TURBOS.IS THE ADDED GAIN REALLY WORTH THE TIME AND MONEY.WHAT KIND OF HORSEPOWER GAINS COULD I EXPECT. I HAVE A 2.8 V6. WHAT KIND OF MODIFICATIONS TO THE ENGINE ARE MADE TO HANDLE THE EXTRA POWER.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||11-12-2000||12:47 AM||||200 horsepower is the minimum you can expect with the 2.8-liter engine. If you keep the boost around 7 lbs. you don't have to do anything to the engine. There are guys here who have put allot of miles on there turbocharged 2.8-liter engines with no problems.<BR> <A HREF="http://designonesystems.com/turbo/index-fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://designonesystems.com/turbo/index-fiero.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||11-12-2000||11:43 AM||||I am in the process of putting a Design1Systems Stage II system in my 1985 GT. I have been working with the owner Kevin and he is very helpful. He estimates the engine to be around 225 hp when it is complete. I bought the kit from someone for $2,700 so it was a pretty good deal. Bang for the buck wise. The engine needs no internal modifications, and the kit comes with a knock sensor to keep it from having problems. It is quite a bit of work installing it if you are like me and not a seasoned mechanic like some of the guys around here, but the instructions are good, and the owner is very patient and helpful with questions over the phone. A new kit will run $3,000 for a Stage one auto and $3,200 for a manual. The reason the manual is more is it comes with a new exhaust system. A stage II kit new costs $3,800 auto and $4,000 for a manual. I have not finished the installation yet so I cannot tell you about the performance, but there is a big difference between 140 and 225 hp. At least that is all I will ever need. I felt it was a good investment considering my Fiero has low mileage on the engine, and a V8 kit with a new engine, plus having to take out a perfectly good V6 was not worth the expense. That is just my opinion though. Not trying to start anything here V8 guys. I wish I had the knowledge and money for a V8 kit and swap. Anyway, good luck if you decide to go the Turbo route. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||martin1875||11-12-2000||02:55 PM||||THANKS FOE THE MUCH NEEDED INFORMATION||||reg||1
